Call at 2:30 PM on a Tuesday

&lt;rings 8 times&gt;

&lt;slow, wooden script reading&gt;

"Hello. You've reached the voice mailbox of XXXXXXX. We are not available at this time. Our business hours at 9-oclock AM to 5-oclock PM, monday through friday. For holiday hours,....."

&lt;30 seconds later&gt; 

"To leave a message, please stay on the line." 

&lt;click, beep, ring x10&gt; 

&lt;new voice&gt;

"This is XXXXX. All our agents are currently busy. Our business hours are...." 

&lt;30 seconds later&gt;

"detailed message with your name, address, phone number, inquiry, and a time of day you would prefer us to call you"

&lt;voicemail tone&gt;

then I leave a long detailed voicemail. Nobody calls back.

Thank you for reaching out to &lt;X&gt; about your concerns. We take all user concerns seriously, especially related to &lt;bad thing we did&gt;. 

To give you some context, &lt;generic platitudes about why the bad thing is ok&gt; 

&lt;assurance that we won't do anything to fix it&gt;

&lt;assurance that we care about you&gt;
